‎## II. THE FOREST
‎
‎**Principle:** Technology is the forest. It doesn't stop growing. Inhabitants survive by adapting.
‎
‎**Evolution visible through coding:**
‎
‎**Law:** Abstraction doesn't remove work. It relocates human effort.
‎
‎- Early: effort close to machine
‎- Later: effort at architecture, integration
‎- Today: effort at intent, verification
‎- Tomorrow: scarce becomes judgment, architecture, problem definition, taste, accountability
‎
‎**Forest keeps changing. Survival problem remains.**
‎
‎> Tools evolve. Ecosystems evolve. Inhabitants evolve. But capacity to issue meaningful command remains. (Dispatch 012 — Rule #13)
‎
‎Inhabitants adapt — or find themselves living in yesterday's ecosystem.
‎
