‎## VI. PRESENT SIGNAL — VAULTED AS OBSERVATION, NOT HYPOTHESIS
‎
‎**Per instruction: Not yet claim about where ChatGPT is going.**
‎
‎**Observation vaulted (Dispatch 017 precursor):**
‎
‎Increasing public discussion around ChatGPT clustering around:
‎- usage limits
‎- degraded/changed performance
‎- model availability
‎- fallback behavior
‎- possibility of moving work between AI systems
‎- budget boundary: cutting all AI spend isn't option, neither is going bankrupt
‎
‎**Interpretation:**
‎Users appear becoming more conscious of infrastructure surrounding AI relationship, rather than evaluating model solely by output quality.
‎
‎User encountering limit: Can I continue?
‎Degraded performance: Can I still trust this tool for my work?
‎Considering migration: Can I take accumulated work somewhere else?
‎Eventually: Which system do I choose?
‎Evaluating gate, not just consuming AI.
‎
‎**Hypothesis — not yet established — needs evidence:**
‎These frictions may be contributing to broader shift toward multi-platform AI use and greater demand for portability.
‎
‎**Historical echo:**
‎Yahoo crossroads wasn't visible because sign said "INTERNET IS CHANGING." Signal distributed across user behavior, technology, competitors, business decisions.
‎
‎Today interesting question: Are ChatGPT users beginning to discover that AI isn't whole system? Once limits, performance, portability, choice become part of conversation, user is no longer merely consuming AI. They're evaluating the gate.
‎
‎**Honesty protocol:** Until evaluation produces behaviour (LOGs), signal, not migration.
